      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "09e08373-774a-592f-84d4-6d49e2467503",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nivek Ogre, Kevin Graham Ogilvie, Frank Sinatra, Martin Atkins, Kevin Crompton, Dave Ogilvie\n- Organizations: Skinny Puppy, Invisible Records\n- Projects: Rx\n- Roles: musician, performance artist, actor, singer, producer\n- Topics: aliases, industrial music\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Sinatra, born Francis Albert Sinatra on December 12, 1915, was an American singer, actor, and producer who became one of the most popular and influential musical artists of the 20th century.\n- Frank Sinatra released his debut album, \"The Voice of Frank Sinatra\", in 1946.\n- Frank Sinatra's career revived in 1953 with the success of \"From Here to Eternity\", and his performance won the Academy Award and Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor.\n- Nivek Ogre, born Kevin Graham Ogilvie on December 5, 1962, is a Canadian musician, performance artist, and actor best known as a founding member of the industrial music group Skinny Puppy.\n- Nivek Ogre used his alias for practical as well as theatrical reasons because Skinny Puppy already included another Kevin, Kevin Crompton, also known as cEvin Key, and was produced by another Ogilvie, Dave Ogilvie, also known as Rave.\n- Rx, also styled as ℞ or Rx, was a one-off side project by Skinny Puppy member Nivek Ogre created in collaboration with Invisible Records founder Martin Atkins.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "33b5adac-0e53-5d70-a2ce-27bc65d4ed5f",
        "text": "Page: Nivek Ogre. Sentence: Nivek Ogre (born Kevin Graham Ogilvie December 5, 1962) is a Canadian musician, performance artist and actor best known as a founding member of the industrial music group Skinny Puppy.\nPage: Nivek Ogre. Sentence: Since that band featured another Kevin (Crompton, a.k.a. cEvin Key) and was produced by another Ogilvie (Dave, a.k.a. Rave), Ogre's alias was practical as well as theatrical.\nPage: Frank Sinatra. Sentence: Francis Albert Sinatra ( ; ] ; December 12, 1915 – May 14, 1998) was an American singer, actor, and producer who was one of the most popular and influential musical artists of the 20th century.\nPage: Frank Sinatra. Sentence: He released his debut album, \"The Voice of Frank Sinatra\", in 1946.\nPage: Frank Sinatra. Sentence: His career was reborn in 1953 with the success of \"From Here to Eternity\", with his performance subsequently winning an Academy Award and Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor.\nPage: Rx (band). Sentence: ℞ or Rx was a one-off side project by Skinny Puppy band member Nivek Ogre, in collaboration with Invisible Records founder Martin Atkins.",
